    "rationale": "GJA5 encodes connexin40, a major atrial gap-junction protein. Pathogenic variants can impair trafficking, channel formation, or intercellular conductance, disrupting cell-to-cell action-potential propagation and predisposing to familial atrial fibrillation. Strongest alternative resolved: Desmosomal mechanical-coupling defects are important in arrhythmogenic cardiomyopathy, but this family has structurally normal hearts and a GJA5 variant reducing connexin40 channels. The direct substrate is impaired low-resistance atrial gap-junction electrical coupling."
